DATA_BLOCK "LOGGING_DB"
TITLE = 'Data Logger Storage Buffer'
// v1.3 changes vs v1.2:
//   - NEW context byte (byte 1 of each record): Machine_Run/Auto_Mode/
//     SystemReset/PotMoved, packed into what was previously a dead
//     alignment-padding byte (needed anyway so the DINTs below start on
//     an even boundary). Zero net record-size change - still compiles
//     to the same 26-byte padded stride FB1111 v1.6 already accounts
//     for. Added to explain WHY reacquisition (ReferenceEstablished)
//     fails to relatch when "RUN_DATA_DB".Alarm sticks on the actual
//     Rotaliner: is the web actually stopped (Machine_Run), is Auto
//     cycling (Auto_Mode falling edge clears ReferenceEstablished), is
//     someone on the pot (PotMoved), or did a SystemReset land mid-fault.
//     Offsets confirmed 2026-08-31 against the online DB600 Address
//     column (Machine_Run 12.0 / Auto_Mode 12.1 / SystemReset 12.2 /
//     PotMoved 12.3) - all four are FB600 VAR_INPUTs, same instance DB
//     FB1111 already has open, no second DB to open.
//   - FB1111 v1.7 companion change: auto-arms LogActive on the rising
//     edge of Alarm (DB600.DBX14.3) instead of requiring the operator
//     to manually catch the fault live. Won't re-arm over an
//     already-running or not-yet-retrieved (LogDone) capture.
//
// v1.2 - fixes a real CPU limit violation in v1.1: the target CPU is a
//   6ES7 315-2AG10-0AB0, max DB size 16KB (16384 bytes). v1.1 (700
//   records x 28 bytes + ~40 bytes header/block overhead = 19640 bytes)
//   exceeded that by over 3KB and would not have compiled/downloaded.
//
//   Two changes bring it back under budget AND improve on v1.1 at the
//   same time:
//
//   1) StateCode, BadStreakCount, MaxBadStreak change from INT (2 bytes
//      each) to BYTE (1 byte each), saving 3 bytes/record. This is safe
//      because all three are confirmed small-bounded values, not
//      general-purpose integers:
//        - StateCode is a 4-value enum (0=None/1=Clean/2=Flick/3=Idle)
//        - BadStreakCount is capped by FB600's own self-healing network
//          (SEAM_CLASSIFY, "Lose Reference OK after repeated bad
//          classifications"): the instant BadStreakCount reaches
//          MaxBadStreak it is reset to 0 in the same scan, so it never
//          runs past MaxBadStreak
//        - MaxBadStreak is a small tunable threshold (documented
//          default 3) - would need to be deliberately reconfigured past
//          255 to overflow a BYTE, which is not a realistic setting
//      FB1111 v1.5 reads these via L DBW (the full INT) then T DIB (a
//      byte-sized destination) - the T instruction naturally takes just
//      the low byte of the loaded value, so no manual byte-offset
//      arithmetic was needed to pick the right half of the source INT.
//
//   2) Record count drops from 700 back to 600, matching DB889's
//      600-record / 30-second capture window exactly. v1.1's 700
//      records (35s) vs DB889's 600 (30s) meant a correlated capture
//      pair would run 5 seconds out of alignment for no real benefit -
//      600/600 lets record index N in one buffer correspond to the same
//      instant as record index N in the other.
//
//   Net: 600 x 25 bytes = 15000 + ~40 bytes overhead = 15040 bytes,
//   comfortably under the 16384-byte limit (~1.3KB spare). Re-verify
//   the actual compiled length against your CPU's real budget before
//   downloading either way - "40 bytes overhead" is an estimate from
//   the v1.1 attempt, not a guaranteed constant.
//
// v1.1 - added BadStreakCount, MaxBadStreak, StateCode as INT fields to
//   directly test the "MaxBadStreak self-healing clears
//   ReferenceEstablished and never recovers" hypothesis for the
//   AGC_Trim lock symptom seen in DB889 (ReferenceEstablished dropped
//   at record 437 and stayed FALSE for the rest of a 30s capture while
//   StFlick kept pulsing). Also corrected 5 pre-existing stale DINT
//   source-offset comments (LastBannerEventCount/LastEncoderPulse/
//   EXPWindow/RefSum/ExpectedNextPulse) that had drifted from FB1111
//   v1.3's already-corrected code. Superseded above by v1.2's BYTE
//   fields and 600-record count - the offset corrections carry forward
//   unchanged.
//
// Record layout v1.3 (still 25 bytes declared / 26 bytes compiled -
// FB1111 v1.6's stride fix already accounts for the padded size, see
// v1.6 header there; the new byte-1 fields fit inside the padding that
// was already forced there for DINT alignment, so nothing about the
// stride changes):
//   Byte 0        : 8 status bits (StNone .0 ... PreviouSeamWasNone .7)
//   Byte 1        : 4 context bits (Machine_Run .0, Auto_Mode .1,
//                   SystemReset .2, PotMoved .3) - NEW v1.3, bits .4-.7
//                   unused (was pure padding pre-v1.3)
//   Bytes 2-5     : LastBannerEventCount (DINT)
//   Bytes 6-9     : LastEncoderPulse (DINT)
//   Bytes 10-13   : EXPWindow (DINT)
//   Bytes 14-17   : RefSum (DINT)
//   Bytes 18-21   : ExpectedNextPulse (DINT)
//   Byte 22       : StateCode (BYTE) - was INT in v1.1
//   Byte 23       : BadStreakCount (BYTE) - was INT in v1.1
//   Byte 24       : MaxBadStreak (BYTE) - was INT in v1.1
//
// 600 records at 50ms/scan = 30 seconds per capture - matches DB889
// exactly for correlated captures.
VERSION : 1.3


  STRUCT 	
   Index : INT  := 1;	// Active tracking write pointer (1 to 1200)
   LogActive : BOOL ;	// Set to TRUE to start recording data
   LogDone : BOOL ;	// Turns TRUE automatically when buffer fills up
   Reset_Log : BOOL ;	// Pulse TRUE to clear all old log data
   Buffer : ARRAY  [1 .. 600 ] OF STRUCT 	// 30 seconds at 50ms intervals
    StNone : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 14.0
    StClean : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 14.1
    StFlick : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 14.2
    Alarm : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 14.3
    RefEstablished : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 14.4
    FirstPulse : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 28.0
    ExpectedPositionValid : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 58.0
    PreviouSeamWasNone : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 64.0
    Machine_Run : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 12.0 - NEW v1.3
    Auto_Mode : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 12.1 - NEW v1.3
    SystemReset : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 12.2 - NEW v1.3
    PotMoved : BOOL ;	// DB600.DBX 12.3 - NEW v1.3
    LastBannerEventCount : DINT ;	// DB600.DBD 20
    LastEncoderPulse : DINT ;	// DB600.DBD 24
    EXPWindow : DINT ;	// DB600.DBD 30
    RefSum : DINT ;	// DB600.DBD 34
    ExpectedNextPulse : DINT ;	// DB600.DBD 54
    StateCode : BYTE ;	// DB600.DBW 66 (low byte) - value range 0-3
    BadStreakCount : BYTE ;	// DB600.DBW 70 (low byte) - bounded by MaxBadStreak
    MaxBadStreak : BYTE ;	// DB600.DBW 72 (low byte) - small config threshold
   END_STRUCT ;	
  END_STRUCT ;	
BEGIN
   Index := 1; 
   LogActive := FALSE; 
   LogDone := FALSE; 
   Reset_Log := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].StNone := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].StClean := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].StFlick := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].Alarm := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].RefEstablished := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].FirstPulse := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].ExpectedPositionValid := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].PreviouSeamWasNone := FALSE; 
   Buffer[1].Machine_Run := FALSE; 
